Clicking "Запази промените" only staged in-memory changes, requiring a separate "Запиши промените" click to actually hit the API. Additionally, save-all-btn must not disturb the currently open product modal or its active inner tab.

## Changes

- **`save-modal-btn` handler** — replaces the stale `showNotification` prompt ("click save-all to store") with an `await saveData()` call, so the form callback → in-memory update → API persist happens atomically in one click
- **`saveData()` (save-all-btn path)** — unchanged; already does not call `renderAll()` or touch modal/tab state, so the open product editor and its selected tab survive a save-all click untouched

```js
// Before
if (success) {
    setUnsavedChanges(true);
    renderAll();
    showNotification('Промените са запазени. Натиснете "Запази всичко" за да ги съхраните.', 'success');
}

// After
if (success) {
    setUnsavedChanges(true);
    renderAll();
    await saveData();   // persists immediately; saveData() emits its own success/error notification
}
```

`setUnsavedChanges(true)` before `saveData()` is intentional — `saveData()` guards with `if (!unsavedChanges) return` and calls `setUnsavedChanges(false)` on success.

