`updateItemBuilder` was calling `chatsForFolder.indexOf(chat)` — an O(n) linear scan — for every updated item, causing lag on large chat lists and undermining the optimization goals of the parent PR.

## Changes

- **`chats_list_page.dart`**: After `_buildSortedList()`, build an `idToIndex` map in a single O(n) pass; use it for O(1) index lookups in `updateItemBuilder`.

```dart
final idToIndex = {
  for (var i = 0; i < chatsForFolder.length; i++) chatsForFolder[i].id: i,
};

// Before
updateItemBuilder: (context, animation, chat) {
  return widget.buildChatListItem(chat, chatsForFolder.indexOf(chat), widget.folder);
}

// After
updateItemBuilder: (context, animation, chat) {
  return widget.buildChatListItem(chat, idToIndex[chat.id] ?? 0, widget.folder);
}
```

